WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
A volcanic eruption is a geological phenomenon,

00:04.000 --> 00:07.000
characterized by violent eruptions on the Earth's surface,

00:08.000 --> 00:11.000
by a volcano, of lava or tephra accompanied by volcanic gases.

00:12.000 --> 00:15.000
Geysers are excluded from this definition

00.16.000 --> 00:19.000
that emit hot water, and the mud volcanoes

00:20.000 --> 00:22.000
whose material is largely organic.
